From: Sungsu Ahn <sungsu_ahn@korea.ac.kr>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:10:22 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 35/51] objects: per-thread coherence instrumentation (MOT1 v6,
 build 71; no protocol change)

Observation only: the coherence protocol, its checks, flushes and retries are
unchanged. Adds per-thread accounting of the object API's coherence time,
read through rackobj::GetObjectThreadCoh (field order = shim CohSnap v2):

- read sections: section checks timed 1 in MEGALON_COH_CHECK_SAMPLE (default
  64); (A) stale copy at read_start and (B) concurrent write at read_end split
  (read_retry_incoherent = read_retry_stale + read_retry_concurrent, v1 field
  kept); (C) META_OUTDATE; (D) contended waits: read_seqlock_begin while odd,
  NR read-side combiner-lock waits and replica RwLock read waits
  (nr/waitstat.rs, per-thread totals via nr_thread_wait_stat).
- write sections: write start (incl. switch_rw and critical-path reclaim) and
  write end (whole-object flush + write_seq_end, bytes) every time.
- plain rdtsc without fences, ns via the TSC rate measured against
  CLOCK_MONOTONIC; MEGALON_COH_TIMERS=0 disables all timer reads.
- object-test phase 7: each counter moves in a constructed case (stale,
  concurrent, meta, spin, checks, flush, switch_rw); churn writer totals vs
  process stats; OBJECT_TEST_OVERHEAD runs timers on/off alternately.
- NR test waitstat_records_contended_read_lock_only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
